INT. HOSPITAL ROOFTOP HELIPAD - DAWN

Concrete, windsock, a single orange cone. The city spreads below in blue haze. A rusted door clatters open.

DR. NATHANIEL OYELOWO-STRAND (40s, scrubs, blood on one cuff) steps out, breathing. Behind him comes NURSE PHILOMENA BRANDT-ADEYEMI (30s, braids, hospital badge swinging). Nearby, an orderly, GASPAR LINDQVIST-MBEKI (20s, lanky, mop bucket), smokes against the rail.

NATHANIEL
Third night in a row.

PHILOMENA
You keep coming up here.

NATHANIEL
Nobody follows me.

PHILOMENA
I followed you.

GASPAR
So did I. I was here first.

The radio on Philomena's belt crackles.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Trauma Two, inbound helicopter, ETA four minutes. Pediatric, severe burns.

Nathaniel straightens. Philomena grabs the radio.

PHILOMENA
(into radio)
Copy. Pad is clear.

She and Nathaniel look at Gaspar, who drops his cigarette and stamps it out. The windsock snaps taut.

NATHANIEL
Gaspar, the cone.

GASPAR
On it.

He drags the orange cone aside. In the distance, a speck grows into the rising hammer of rotors.
